extraction_notes: "WB20 Canada printed 84-85 (cache p085-p086, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer; both pages were rendered and read beside it. Heading Tundra Ranger O.C.C. on printed 84, stat block headed Tundra Ranger Soldier/Lawman O.C.C. (also known as the Peacekeeper and Avenging Ranger); the O.C.C. Skills list runs over onto printed 85. || GROUP: the book has no Men at Arms heading; the chapter is The Tundra Rangers (printed 78-90) and the entry calls the character a dedicated soldier and lawman of a para-military force, so occ_group is men-of-arms and men_of_arms is true. The entry prints no S.D.C. base; +5D6+10 S.D.C. is listed under O.C.C. bonuses and is stored as a pool bonus. || XP: the Tundra Ranger, Headhunter Techno-Hound and Trapper-Woodsman ladder on printed 192, as supplied from a render. || BONUSES: +1 P.E. and +1D4 P.S. (text layer +lD4), +1 attack per melee, +2 initiative, +1 roll, +2 pull punch, +2 vs pain stored; +1 vs cold is stored as saves.other; +1 vs Horror Factor at levels 2, 4, 7, 10 and 13 as five at_level entries. || SKILL READINGS: Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic; Speaks American/English at 98% is Language: Native Tongue; Literate in American at 84% +1% per level is Literacy: Native Language at 84 with per_level 1; Pilot: Hover Vehicle is Hover Craft (ground); Tracking (humanoids) is Tracking (people); Swim and Climb are Swimming and Climbing. Pilot one of choice, any except robots and aircraft, is a Pilot pick excluding the robot, power armor, aircraft and spacecraft rows. Hand to Hand: Expert, Martial Arts or Assassin (if Anarchist or evil) for one related skill, CS Commando for two; CS Commando is the catalog row Hand to Hand: Commando. || RELATED: Electrical Basic only is Basic Electronics; Science is Astronomy and Mathematics: Advanced; Pilot except robots, ships and aircraft excludes the robot and power armor rows, Boat: Ships, the submersible and warship rows, and every aircraft and spacecraft row; Jet Packs, hovercycles and Military: Tanks & APCs stay available (a reading). This book files riding under Pilot, so the catalog Horsemanship category is offered as General and Exotic Animals only; Cowboy: none keeps Horsemanship: Cowboy out. || EQUIPMENT: Standard Equipment, Vehicle and Money all say Standard and point at Notes on the Tundra Rangers, printed 82-83, so that list is stored: Legion Tundra armor and the thermal-armor suit (catalog rows from this book), six E-Clips, a Vibro-Blade as a pick of three since the book names no kind, two field uniforms, a dress uniform, cleated insulated combat boots, casual and dress clothing, thermal gloves on the plain gloves row, the high-impact helmet with built-in communicator on the communications-helmet row, tinted goggles, the 100 feet of nylon cord on the cord row, utility belt, scarf, air filter, backpack, bedroll, duffle bag or saddlebag as a pick, flashlight, distancing binoculars, language translator, note pad, 1D4 markers, 1D4 signal flares, two canteens, 6 weeks of rations as six of the week-sized food-rations row, first aid kit, and a horse or hovercycle as a pick (printed 83: a horse or hovercycle are pretty standard). NOT stored, no catalog row: the energy rifle itself and one weapon with two E-Clips for each W.P. (the book names no models; printed 187 points at the core book early Coalition weapons), dress boots, pick-hatchet, tundra survival kit, 20 climbing anchors, small M.D.C. ceramic mallet, web vest, winter cap. The multi-optics goggle is a special request, not issue, and is left out. || MONEY: Standard is a salary of 1500 credits per month plus room, board and gear (printed 83); the book prints no starting savings, so one month of salary is stored as starting_money, a reading. || The Code of the Tundra Rangers (printed 81) is paraphrased in the body."
---

## Lore

The Tundra Rangers are what became of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police. A
few thousand Mounties and soldiers gathered at an experimental military
super-base near Fort Smith after the Great Cataclysm, and then the whole
installation slipped out of time; they woke to find some 265 years gone and
the world in ruins. They chose to carry on anyway, as an independent
peacekeeping force with no government behind it.

A Ranger of this O.C.C. is the classic one: part frontier lawman, part
commando. Training favors small teams and precise work, such as getting into
a stronghold, sabotage, rescue and breaking up an enemy before the main
assault, over holding a battle line. They ride circuit through western and
northern Canada in pairs or small squads, visiting towns, ranches, trading
posts and tribes, settling disputes, running down criminals and killing the
monsters that come out of the Calgary Rift.

Off duty a Ranger may be a loud practical joker; with civilians, courteous
and kind; in a fight, cold and methodical, with the safety of bystanders
first and little mercy for the guilty. Their white armor and red maple leaf
are trusted across the north, and people say they always get their man.

## The Code of the Tundra Rangers

- Keep the people of Canada safe, and keep the peace.
- See tyranny for what it is, whatever shape it takes, and stand against it.
- Help and protect those who need it, but leave them able to manage for
  themselves; that is the best help there is.
- Never let up in the pursuit of justice. The guilty answer for what they did.
- Welcome other beliefs and ways of living, and value what all peaceful,
  thinking beings share.
- Do not doubt the good being done. Believe in yourself and others will too.
- Make no threat or demand that you cannot and will not back with force.
- Keep your word and never betray a trust; the trust people give the Rangers
  is worth more than any reward.
- Never compromise a fellow Ranger, and never speak for another.
- One person can change things.
- No Tundra Ranger stands alone.

## GM Notes

Standard issue the sheet does not list, because the catalog has no row for it:
the energy rifle itself, a weapon for every W.P. with two E-Clips apiece, dress
boots, a pick-hatchet, a tundra survival kit, 20 climbing anchors, a small
M.D.C. ceramic mallet, a web vest and a winter cap. Many Rangers also wear a
multi-optics goggle, by special request.

Heavier weapons, armor, power armor, explosives, sensors, generators and
extra supplies may be issued for a particular assignment, at the commanding
officer''s discretion. Veterans collect personal non-standard gear as well.

Pay is 1500 credits a month on top of room, board, medical care and
equipment, and rises with rank and hazard duty (the book points at Coalition
War Campaign pages 50-54 for rank and pay). The sheet starts the character
with one month of salary.

A Ranger checks in at a station at least every two months and returns to
Regina or the Fort Smith headquarters at least once a year. Breaking the Code
or disobeying orders means a dishonorable discharge.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'tundra-ranger');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'tundra-ranger';

